-- Q3827: IT General Controls [medium/L2]
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Program change management controls","Logical access and authentication controls","Business continuity and disaster recovery controls","User provisioning and deprovisioning controls"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): A data center failure directly tests business continuity and disaster recovery (BC/DR) controls. Per COBIT 2019 DSS04 (Manage Continuity), BC/DR controls include offsite backups, alternate processing facilities, documented recovery procedures, and defined RTO/RPO objectives. These controls specifically ensure the organization can resume critical operations after catastrophic infrastructure failure.
Wrong (A): Program change management governs modifications to applications and systems, not recovery from infrastructure disasters.
Wrong (B): Logical access controls restrict system authentication and authorization, which are unrelated to disaster recovery operations.
Wrong (D): User provisioning manages account creation and removal lifecycle, not organizational resilience to data center outages.$EXPL$
